      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a4b034d1ab4366d42644996|full_name}: Lobby isn't the right term for instances in VRC. Usually in games the lobby would be where players meet up before entering a game. Players in FPS games will be sitting in the lobby together chatting while the map is voted on, in RTS games the lobby is where you pick your faction/race before getting into the game itself, and so on.\nIn VRC you don't really have a lobby. You could enter an instance and treat it like a lobby I suppose. \"Everyone meet at The Box while we decide where to drop the next portal.\" That just feels wrong though.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
